---
// The actual deployment-topology diagram from Shelfinity's own README
// (docs/images/deployment-models.svg), reused as-is rather than redrawn.
---

<figure class="arch">
	<img
		src="/projects/shelfinity-deployment-models.svg"
		alt="Diagram of Shelfinity's three deployment models: Local runs the app, Postgres, and Keycloak as containers on one machine. Hybrid runs the app locally against real IBM Cloud Db2 and App ID. Multi-cloud, the production setup, routes through Cloudflare's tunnel to an Oracle Cloud Infrastructure VM running the app and reading secrets from OCI Vault, which talks to IBM Cloud Db2 and App ID."
		width="1120"
		height="870"
		loading="lazy"
		decoding="async"
	/>
</figure>

<style>
	.arch {
		margin: 0;
		width: 100%;
	}

	img {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		display: block;
		background: #fff;
		border-radius: calc(var(--radius) - 1px);
	}
</style>
